englishText:
A faceless warrior's sword, destining him to fall. ^green;Hold SHIFT to parry^white;.

^yellow;Channeled Fury: 1.5x damage on the first and final 3 strikes.^white;
^red;Poor Maintenance: No knockback on all other attacks.^white;

A modern Peasant's battle axe, more akin to a hatchet than anything else. The light build of this weapon allows faster attacks than its Warrior counterpart. ^green;Hold SHIFT to parry^white;.

^yellow;Last Resort: 50hp blocking power.^white;
^yellow;Warrior's Multi-tool: One-handed.^white;
^green;Invasion Mindset: 3x damage on first strike.^white;

A Floran copy of a Hylotl Katana, wielded by privileged warriors loyal (or that used to be loyal) to a Greenfinger. Its presence suggests Florans engaged in some manner of cultural appropriation. ^green;Its attacks may overwhelm the melee defenses of false Floran martial artists^white;.

^yellow;Ancient Arsenal: 100hp blocking power.^white;
^green;Unremarkable: Reliable and balanced two-handed sword.^white;

A well-rounded versatile sword of non-descript make suited for use alongside Buckler Shields. Swords like these are rare amongst a galaxy filled with firearms, but when the bullets run dry and the guns have melted, a sharp pointy stick will never let you down. ^green;Hold SHIFT to parry^white;.

^yellow;En Garde!: 200hp blocking power.^white;
^yellow;Men-at-Arms: One-handed.^white;

A traditional sword notably requested by Unitan Officers for morale purposes. Hails from Earth's ''Graveyard of Empires''. Benefits those willing to give an enemy a taste of their steel before the target can react. ^green;Hold SHIFT to parry^white;.

^yellow;Mass-Produced: 100hp blocking power.^white;
^yellow;Modern Craftsmanship: One-handed.^white;
^green;Aggressive Intent: Increased knockback and damage with each phase of combo, up to 1.7x.^white;

The term naginata first appeared in historical documents in the Heian period (794-1185). The earliest clear references to naginata date from 1146. In Honchō Seiki compiled from 1150 to 1159 in the late Heian period, it is recorded that Minamoto no Tsunemitsu mentioned that his weapon was a naginata.
^#B10000;Formation-Breaker: Similar range to the Soldier's Halberd but with faster attack speed and higher knockback.^white;
^#00DDEE;Heian Alien, Heian Weapon: SHIFT to bash a target, stunning them for a superior 3s, at the cost of a longer cooldown than usual.^white;

----^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;
^yellow;Advanced Spear Techniques: 50hp blocking HP | 0.4s Perfect Parry | 0.5s parry cooldown.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;Terco: [SHIFT] to make a quick overhead thrust, dealing heavy boss bleed and regular bleeding, stunning for 2 seconds.^reset;

''You should not have a favourite weapon. To become over-familiar with one weapon is as much a fault as not knowing it sufficiently well.'' - Miyamoto Musashi
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;
^orange;Adept Overconfidence: 0.25s PARRY WINDOW.^reset;
^yellow;Noble Vengance: Successful Perfect Blocks will stun nearby combatants and briefly Shade-Step the wielder.^reset;
^blue;Jack-of-All: Tap SHIFT to switch stances, hold SHIFT to use stance-specific abilities.^reset;

An axe that's been designed for adaptive combat, resembling a miniature poleaxe with a spike for thrusting and an axe-head for heavy cleaves. A cunning weapon for a cunning lot, this axe makes up for its poor range with its fast quickstep ability and decent striking speed.
^orange;Back, foul beast!: 2x damage on first strike. Heavy knockback on final attack. Inflicts BOSS-BLEED.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Quickstep: [SHIFT] to initiate a rapid double-dash forwards to get around targets or make a quick escape | 1s cooldown.

The Daimyo's personal sword. A well-maintained piece of equipment. ^green;Hold SHIFT to parry^white;.

^yellow;Channeled Fury: 1.5x damage on the first and final 3 strikes.^white;
^red;Poor Maintenance: No knockback on all other attacks.^white;

The greatsword of an Erchius Warrior, a man who was so honorbound upon his assimilation that he remained vigilant at his post. He would be bested by an adventurer, and unceremoniously replaced by the Banner-Bearers of the Erchius.
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to block.^white;
^orange;Blunt Trauma: 2s STUN and +250 TRUE DMG for every attack.^white;
^yellow;Incomprehensible Strength: [SHIFT] to initiate an uninterruptable heavy cleave.^white;

''I would rather betray the world, than have the world betray me.''

^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;
^yellow;Youkai's Resolve: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY | Parry hitbox is larger than usual.^white;

^#D6DFFF;Amanojaku's Uprising: [SHIFT] to activate weapon's special ability. Drain 250HP but also gain +90% DMG RES over 20s | 30s cooldown.^white;

The longsword was a quick, effective, and versatile weapon capable of deadly thrusts, slices, and cuts. The longsword is characterized not so much by a longer blade, but by a longer grip, which indicates a weapon designed for two-handed use.
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;

^yellow;Riposte: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 150HP STABILITY.^reset;
^orange;Hardened Steel: [SHIFT] to hilt bash nearby targets, stunning them for two seconds.^reset;

An otherwise unremarkable spear of standard-make. The Clacton Spear found in England and the Schöningen spears found in Terran-Germany documents that wooden spears have been used for hunting since at least 400 000 years ago.

^#D1C8BF;+25 TRUE DMG for standard attacks.

^#D6DFFF;Press [SHIFT] to initiate a charged thrust, dashing forward and dealing additional damage against [GiC] bosses.^white;

Self-defence precision sword popular in the hands of civilians and military personnel alike. Very fast thrust attacks, but demands more aim-control from its user.
^yellow;Precision Strikes: Thrust Attacks deal 2.0x damage.^white;

^#D6DFFF;Focused Thrust: Press [SHIFT] to initiate a charged thrust, charging forward and dealing additional damage against [GiC] bosses^white; | ^#D6DFFF;+100% DODGE and Knockback Resistance when readying a charge.^white;

A sealed crate of workplace Industrial Equipment, serving its roles in the heavy industry sector of humanity.

Deliver to an Extraction Colony for profit.

^#775526;There's some strong packaging keeping this crate together. It's probably best not to open it unless you really want everything inside or don't mind being wasteful...^reset;

A weapon utilized by those who like to bring a little spice to the battlefield. Awkward to use. ^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry^reset;

^#006847;Men Among Beasts: 150hp blocking power with 0.45s Perfect Parry.^reset;
^#FFFFFF;Gunpowder-Hunter: Holding SHIFT then releasing SHIFT fires a shotgun charge within the spear, or pumps the spear to ready the next round. ^red;Tapping SHIFT will reload your spear with 18.5x70mm Buckshot shotgun shells.^reset;

A Medical Kit offering the ^yellow;bare minimum equipment^white; deemed ^green;safe^white; by the Galactic Community. Covers most broad types of injuries. Not intended for military use.

^green;- Restores 100 health/4s | Heal Delay: 1s | Slowdown Time: 2s
^orange;- Stops Bleeding.^white;

''Just as sure as Rome is falling. I'll be rising again.''

Many Celestials are often depicted as having fallen from grace, casting away their heavenly duties. Others, however, choose to throw themselves out to live (and perhaps love) amongst mortals.

^#87B31B;Celestial Grace: [SHIFT] to initiate an AoE 100HP Group Heal, healing [ALL] units within a small area.^reset;

''Stop playing with yourselves. We've got ground to take.''

A brew originating from the planet of Gazri in commemoration of the workers who toiled to build the great planet.

^Green;-50% Fall Damage for 1 hour.^reset;

''If you seek Him, He will let you find Him; but if you forsake Him, He will reject you forever.''

^green;Hold [SHIFT] to parry.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Peasant Origins: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 10HP STABILITY.^white;
^green;Strike True: 3x damage on first strike. Inflicts special bleed damage against [GiC] Bosses.^white;

A Greenfinger's trophy. It was kept as an heirloom, signifying the time Hylotl Assassins failed to eliminate the Floran's ancestors during a dark age of conquest. ^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;

^green;Belligerent Nobility: 0.45s PARRY WINDOW | 150HP STABILITY.^white;
^yellow;Light Flurry: Extremely fast attacks.^white;
^green;Sharpened Steel: SHIFT to initiate a counter that inflicts special boss bleeding if executed correctly.^reset;
^Red;1st attack enrages enemies (5s), increasing their attack power.^white;

Apparently the creation of a pure-fairy workforce. Apparently.

^orange;Grants SECOND-CHANCE for 30 minutes.^reset;

^#96CBE7;SECOND CHANCE - On taking FATAL Damage, gain 3s of INVULNERABILITY^reset;

''Bring it on, rabbit-boy.''

A special variant of sake fermented by the Lunarians. Despite claims that only the Lunarians could create such a drink, this has been proven false by both Earth-Rabbits and Cletus from your local farmstead.

^#EDC078;0.5x Gravity Modifier for 15 minutes.^reset;

Specialized smoke munitions that can be loaded into a grenade launcher.

^orange;Player Effects: Grants immunity to BALLISTIC DMG, removes SUPPRESSION, +60% DODGE, and cripples ranged weapons. Lasts for 40 seconds after detonation.^reset;
^#FFDD00;Infantry Effects: Causes PANIC for 5s. Affected Infantry will run wildly and hesitate to shoot. Veteran infantry are not affected by PANIC. Does not affect monsters/bosses.^reset;

''Nothing has changed. No task is complete. And after I am gone, what then?''

''It is a chronicle of Gensokyo. It will include my life as the only Judge. It will not be written that the Goddess of Judgment stood on one man's shoulder many times. But I know it to be true.''

^orange;Summon [5x Undead Archers]: [SHIFT] to summon a small team that fights for you. Lasts 60s if not taking damage^white; | ^orange;70s cooldown.^white;

''To seek the Creator was our purpose. Everything we did was in pursuit of finding the truth of His Creation. Yet all we found was more silence.''

A substance held within a vial that seems to clear the mind considerably. Whether it's advanced chemicals or actual magic, there is no doubt that these vials could be useful.

^orange;Staves off the addictions of archetypes for 15 minutes.^white;

A seemingly broken sword wielded by gifted Druflorans. When wielded, the blade is restored to its full glory. Rise from the ashes and ^#D96045;deal FIRE damage on strikes^white;.

^yellow;March of the Meek: Able to ignite oil-coated targets on any hit.^white;
^#D96045;Manifest Destiny: [SHIFT] to initiate a heavy attack with a ranged fire projectile. Press [SHIFT] again to combo into a second heavy attack.^reset;

''Steel is still steel.''

^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;
^yellow;Mirage: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY.^white;
^#E2006D;Purification: Nullifies [Vanilla] ARMOR and psychically grounds anomalies for 15 seconds.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Maiden's War Spirit: [SHIFT] to channel the weapon's memories. Creates homing talismans when its bearer is damaged for up to 60s | 120s cooldown.^reset;

''A small force which is highly trained in the conflicts of war is more apt to victory; a raw and untrained horde is always exposed to slaughter.''
^orange;On use: [EWS/GiC] LIGHT and MEDIUM WEAPON/ARMOR movement penalties are negated.^reset;
^yellow;TRAITS are semi-permanent buffs granted to the player at either an Altar of Hope, or through the Colonial Bioengineer. A player afflicted with a TRAIT will retain that buff until death or manual removal.^reset;

A gigantic sewing needle that serves as a Rapier-type weapon. Can be thrown at foes to bring them closer towards the user. Not usable in the creation of clothing.

^#D6DFFF;Kobito of the Shining Needle: Hold and release [SHIFT] to throw. When thrown, deal 10 DMG, but any hit enemies are pulled towards the user and STUNNED for 3s.^reset;

^green;Inchling: While thrown, press [SHIFT] to forcibly recall the rapier.^reset;

''It's not size that counts in an army, but skill. It's not prowess that counts in a General, but finesse.''

^orange;Rally [3x Jiangshi Fire-Lancers]: [SHIFT] to summon three temporary allies that fight for you. Lasts 60s if not taking damage^white; | ^orange;120s cooldown.^white;
^red;- Tool does nothing else.^reset;

''The courage of a soldier is heightened by his knowledge of his profession.''
^orange;On use: Unaffected by Greatshield Formation penalties | [EWS/GiC] MEDIUM Armor Weight penalties are negated.^reset;
^yellow;TRAITS are semi-permanent buffs granted to the player at either an Altar of Hope, or through the Colonial Bioengineer. A player afflicted with a TRAIT will retain that buff until death or manual removal.^reset;

The katana of a former Protector who performed the Ruin lobotomization ritual, as untold numbers had done before him. He was no different than the rest.
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to block^reset;

^#5CAAD1;Arcane Ark: Each attack phase deals different status effects. ^Red;Final attack enrages enemies, increasing their attack power.^white;
^yellow;Quickdraw: SHIFT to trigger an iaijutsu attack. If hit while performing the attack, counter with a strong downslash.

''There is an art to leading peasants.''

A crudely-maintained Gunbai originally used by Hylotl troops during the Hylotl-Floran War. The FLF seem to have a keen interest in these items.
^#D6DFFF;Rally [Yari + Musketeer + Cannoneer]: [SHIFT] to summon three temporary allies that fight for you. Lasts 80s if not taking damage^white; | ^#D6DFFF;100s cooldown.^white;
^red;- Tool does nothing else.^reset;

A simple spear that's taken clear design influences from another time. A dextrous wielder can use this effectively, regardless of their skill in sojutsu. ^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;

^yellow;Heaven's Reach: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY.^white;
^green;Hunter of Shinobi: Final strike is a weaker version of a hilt-bash.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Offensive-Defense: [SHIFT] to initiate a fast retreating slash, stepping forward and then slicing whilst dashing back. Deals 1s boss bleed.^reset;

-Disabled weapon-

^orange;Celestial-Splitter: SHIFT triggers an uninterruptable heavy cleave, dealing heavy damage with extended bleed damage against [GiC] bosses.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Strike True: 3x damage on first strike. Deals 2s BOSS-BLEED and OVERCHARGES targets (-50% ATK).^reset;^white;

A pike is effectively an extremely long spear. It might seem comical as it is unwieldy in single duels and in close-quarters environments. ^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;

^yellow;Advanced Pike Techniques: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 50HP STABILITY | 0.5s PARRY COOLDOWN | Parry hitbox is closer to the blade and does not protect at close-ranges.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;Tercio: [SHIFT] to make a quick overhead thrust, dealing heavy boss bleed and regular bleeding, stunning for 2 seconds.^reset;

''You want to redefine yourself, kid? Go ahead. Change is a sign of growth after all...''

^orange;On use: Clears ALL TRAITS and QUIRKS from the character.^reset;

^yellow;This will clear all traits and quirks gained from Altars of Hope or Colonial Bioengineers. Altars of Hope will always yield positive buffs, but some QUIRKS granted by Colonial Bioengineers may be too much for the affected to bear...^reset;

''I do not carry the sword because I find it practical. I carry it in memory of our past. Do not forget that your privileges were granted by men who died for them.''
^green;Hold SHIFT to block.^white;
^yellow;Officer's Advance: 150HP STABILITY | Slow for its class | Cannot parry.^white;
^orange;Unbroken: Lethal Bullets do not nullify previously-applied bandages, allowing bandages to resist bleed damage without requiring reapplication during combat.^reset;

''What do you mean 50 STR to wield this?''

^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to block.^white;

^orange;Serrated Edge: Regular attacks inflict additional heavy bleed damage against regular enemies and [GiC] Bosses | 500HP STABILITY.^white;
^yellow;Incomprehensible Strength: [SHIFT] to initiate an uninterruptable heavy cleave, dealing 5s BOSS-BLEED.^white;

''To the line! TO THE LINE!''

^orange;On use: +50% Knockback Resistance until death or removal.^reset;

^yellow;TRAITS are semi-permanent buffs granted to the player at either an Altar of Hope, or through the Colonial Bioengineer. A player afflicted with a TRAIT will retain that buff until death or manual removal.^reset;

''If you stay, then you pay.''

^#E2006D;Multiversal Shattering: Negates [Vanilla] ARMOR value for 5s.^white;
^yellow;Killing blows on most anomalies confer microcredits.^white;

^#D6DFFF;Landlord's Lash Out: [SHIFT] to channel the weapon's spirit, gaining immense resistance to anomalies for 15s | 40s cooldown. Interrupts hilt-bashes of other weapons.^reset;

A small handaxe typically used as a tool for cutting wood although often found in lesser-developed areas. Despite its extremely poor range, one who lets slip the dogs of war will find themselves coursing with new-found power!

^green;Northern Affinity: 3x damage on first strike | All attacks afflict BOSS-BLEED against [GiC] Bosses.^white;

^#D6DFFF;War Cry: [SHIFT] to gain +90% DMG RES for 7s | 40s cooldown.

''I thought that my destiny was to return to my home. I've lost my lands. I've lost my name. I can no longer call myself alive...''

Something that cannot be defined... The power of a sun contained within an unstable field, attached to a pole.

^orange;Hitting an enemy will cause a large explosion.^white;

''From the lowliest of sheets meant to keep a man from freezing to death, to the extravagant rugs of a high noble's household- Fabrics and textiles permeate our lives.''

^orange;UNLOCKS: Conversion of specific [GiC] Clothing Articles into [Vanilla] Fabric at [Hand-Crafting] if [FABRIC] is not already unlocked.^reset;

This also unlocks any crafting recipes that directly produce [Vanilla] Fabric.

''Don't get shot... and good luck.''

A standard glass of Letty Lager, a common brand aboard the Gazring Station. A low-to-nonexistent alcohol content enables even stoic drinkers to revel in social drinking.

^orange;+25 MAX HP when below 50% HP | Additional +50 MAX HP when below 25% HP | Lasts 30 minutes.^reset;

''I'm not fond of blood, but at least it's yours.''

^orange;On use: +15% BLEED Resistance until death or removal.^reset;

^yellow;TRAITS are semi-permanent buffs granted to the player at either an Altar of Hope, or through the Colonial Bioengineer. A player afflicted with a TRAIT will retain that buff until death or manual removal.^reset;

''Farewell to those heavens
Goodbye, the world I knew
Seen enough of old legends
Time to see new tales through.''

^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry | 0.4s PARRY WINDOW.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;Backstep Thrust: [SHIFT] to initiate a rapid back-step then forward-thrust. Deals 2s BOSS-BLEED and OVERCHARGES targets (-50% ATK).^reset;

''Oh, my dear Mankind has learnt so much with this fire. Oh how I wish they hadn't!''

A common torch formed by wrapping a drenched cloth around the end of a wooden stick.
^#D6DFFF;The Fire: Enemies hit by the torch are set alight.^white;

^#FDD14D;The Hunt: Enemies afflicted by OIL-COATING are set alight to greater effect^white; | ^orange;1s STUN per hit.^white;

''Come on, 'Tengu'. Are you a beast, or do you yearn to live the life of humanity?''

A small drink with a light amber color and a very high alcohol content. Whilst originally a closely-guarded secret, there's not much to boast about when your entire species is nearly extinct. And so, its recipe was taught to human brewers.

^#EDC078;+10% Movement Speed for 30 minutes.^reset;

''Fight not for glory and fame.''

^orange;On use: +20% Psychic Resistance until death or removal.^reset;

^yellow;TRAITS are semi-permanent buffs granted to the player at either an Altar of Hope, or through the Colonial Bioengineer. A player afflicted with a TRAIT will retain that buff until death or manual removal.^reset;

''I will wait for her. I will give all of my life to her. She is here, yet not here... I know she awaits her time, too.''

A Soldier's Longsword with added weight in the hilt, allowing for an alternative method of bashing foes. ^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;
^yellow;Riposte: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 150HP STABILITY.^reset;

^orange;Weighted Pommel: SHIFT to charge a heavy hilt bash, stunning enemies for 1.5 seconds. Unaffected by Hilt Bash cooldowns.^reset;

A traditional non-descript sword of unknown make with a broken blade. Completely covered in rust, its sharpness is negligible. Only the mad, undying, or disgraced would fight with this.
^green;Scavenger Roots: 2x damage on non-shove attacks. Final attack shoves enemies away.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Lunge: [SHIFT] to initiate a dash forwards, followed by a strong upwards thrust which deals bleeding against [GiC] bosses and regular enemies. Only, it will not look very impressive with a broken sword. 3s cooldown.

''Pity those who believe themselves strong yet pale when faced with oblivion, for their strength is a mockery, and all who follow them will be ash in the wind. Forgotten.''

^green;Hold and release [SHIFT] to throw the Javelin.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;The Teachings of the Cult: Extremely fast for its weapon class.^reset;

In a world of madness and ghosts, one man had a simple rule for any entity, dead or alive, that resided on his property:
''IF YOU STAY, THEN YOU PAY.''
^#E2006D;Multiversal Shattering: Obliterates a target's defenses for 5 seconds.^white;
^yellow;Material Freebooter: Killing blows on most anomalies confers microcredits as loot.^white;

''I'm here to march against the force of evil! Here to die in the pouring rain!''

^orange;On use: +10% Speed until death or removal.^reset;

^yellow;TRAITS are semi-permanent buffs granted to the player at either an Altar of Hope, or through the Colonial Bioengineer. A player afflicted with a TRAIT will retain that buff until death or manual removal.^reset;

'Komplekt Medecinskih Pripasov', meaning 'Medical Supply Pack' was an early miniature first aid kit issued to colonists since the first days of large-scale space travel.

^green;- Restores 50 health/2s | Heal Delay: 0.5s | Slowdown Time: 1.5s
^orange;- Stops Bleeding.^white;

A traditional sword notably requested by Unitan Officers for morale purposes. Hails from Earth's ''Graveyard of Empires''. This sword embodies power in its first strike, but subsequent strikes will falter. ^green;Hold SHIFT to parry^white;.
^yellow;Infantryman's Best Friend: 150hp blocking power.^white;
^yellow;Modern Craftsmanship: One-handed.^white;
^green;Shoddy Ergonomics: First strike starts at 5x damage. ^yellow;Attacking continously will result in weaker attacks.^white;

Demilitarization and disarmament of Earth at the onset of the Protectorate's reign was a smooth transition under the guise of imposing the ''cultural'' weapons of the undesirable alien refugees dumped there by other stellar empires (Apex Rebels, Avian Grounded, Floran pacifists, and especially non-gestalt Glitch).
^green;Hardened Steel: [SHIFT] to hilt bash nearby targets, stunning them for two seconds.^reset;
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;
^yellow;Riposte: 150hp blocking power with 0.4s Perfect Parry.^reset;

